---
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { GITHUB_REPO } from '../../lib/repo.ts';
import { CURRENT_VERSION } from '../../lib/versions.ts';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const u = (r: string) => base.replace(/\/$/, '') + r;
---

<Layout
  title="About the Lab"
  description="How the Adaptive AI Lab works: playbook → projects → evidence → evolution, and what is normative where."
  section="about"
>
  <header class="doc-head">
    <div class="doc-eyebrow">
      <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />
    </div>
    <h1>About the lab</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      The <strong>Adaptive AI Lab</strong> develops and validates the
      <a href={u('/playbook/')}>Adaptive AI Systems Playbook</a> — an evidence-driven,
      project-independent methodology for building AI systems. The playbook is the lab's product.
      Everything else exists to make it trustworthy.
    </p>

    <h2>The loop</h2>
    <p>
      The lab runs <em>real project implementations</em>, harvests their frozen experimental evidence
      into <a href={u('/cases/')}>curated case studies</a>, and promotes what survives into the
      playbook:
    </p>
    <pre class="ascii-diagram">research evidence → playbook → project implementations → primary records
        ↑                                                      ↓
        └──────── playbook evolution ← curated case studies ←──┘</pre>
    <p>
      The first project implementation is <strong>FIS — the Fintech Integration Sandbox</strong>: a
      realistic synthetic fintech laboratory with deterministic ground truth, frozen eval suites, and
      fail-closed cryptographic provenance. It is the empirical source of every real case study shipped
      so far. It is a project <em>in</em> this lab, not the lab itself — which is why its operational
      records appear here only where case-study provenance reaches them, at
      <a href={`${GITHUB_REPO}/tree/main/projects/fis`} rel="noopener"><code>projects/fis/</code></a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Authority in one breath</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>playbook/</code> is normative for reusable methodology (this site renders v{CURRENT_VERSION});</li>
      <li><code>projects/&lt;name&gt;/</code> is normative for that project's plan and execution;</li>
      <li><code>docs/</code> is normative for lab governance;</li>
      <li>frozen records are authoritative for the facts of their own events;</li>
      <li>none of them overrides another in its own domain.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <a href={u('/research/')}>Research reports</a> are evidence, never rules: a report changes nothing
      by itself. Findings reach the playbook only through the promotion path — evidence-map
      adjudication, then a chapter rule with a strength label, then a
      <a href={u('/changelog/')}>changelog</a> entry.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      This site is a <strong>derived presentation layer</strong> for humans: reading, navigation,
      search, cross-referencing, and visual learning over the canonical repository files. It maintains
      no content of its own — every page is generated from the repository's Markdown, YAML, and Git
      history at build time, and every page links back to its canonical source. Historical playbook
      versions are extracted from the exact release commits (see <a href={u('/versions/')}>Versions</a>).
      The repository — not this website — is the evidence of record:
      <a href={GITHUB_REPO} rel="noopener">{GITHUB_REPO.replace('https://', '')}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    Governance details live in the repository's <code>docs/</code> directory — the canonical index is
    <a href={`${GITHUB_REPO}/blob/main/docs/README.md`} rel="noopener">docs/README.md</a>.
  </footer>
</Layout>
